motions.motion_text:
WHEREAS in October 2023 Council approved (ACS2023-IWS-AM-0003) the local improvement project and the associated cost-recovery apportionment and enacted the authorization by-law, By-law 2023-460; and
WHEREAS the Committee of Revision met on February 20, 2026 and adjourned until March 10, 2026 to allow Council consideration of a longer special charge recovery period from 10 years to 20 years, as raised by affected property owners;
WHEREAS at its meeting of 25 February 2026, Council approved a 20-year special charge recovery period for the Taunton Place Sanitary Sewer extension; and
WHEREAS the authority of the Local Improvement Committee of Revision is set out in Ontario Regulation 586/06 of the Municipal Act, 2001.  The Committee of Revision must review any objections submitted by affected homeowners and determine whether any adjustments are required, in accordance with the Regulation.  Once the Committee of Revision approves the Local Improvement Assessment Roll, Council can pass a by-law to impose the charges on the affected properties; and
WHEREAS the Special Assessment Roll for the Taunton Place Sanitary Extension has been revised as a result of Council’s approval of a 20-year special charge recovery period;
THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED THAT Committee of Revision receive and approve the revised Local Improvement Special Assessment Roll for the Taunton Place Sanitary Sewer Extension, as outlined in this reportand as amended pursuant to Council’s approval of a 20-year special charge recovery period, following discussion of the written objection(s) submitted by the affected homeowner(s).
